+# Pre-ship review — USDC Payouts (Base)
+
+Scope: `packages/nextjs` frontend + config. Read-only pass; no code changed.
+`yarn next:check-types` passes — every finding below is runtime behavior, config, or content, not a compile error.
+
+Summary: 10 ship-blocking, 13 should-fix. The `/payouts` page bypasses the scaffold write hook, so it has no
+wrong-network guard, no simulation, no confirmation wait, and no user-visible errors — that cluster (#1–#4) is the
+core risk for real users sending real USDC.
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### 1. Disconnected users get a paragraph, not a Connect button
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:70-71`
+
+`{!isConnected ? <p>Please connect your wallet to send a payout.</p> : ...}` is a dead end. The only connect
+affordance is in the header, which the copy does not point to.
+
+**Fix:** render the real button in the action slot:
+```tsx
+import { RainbowKitCustomConnectButton } from "~~/components/scaffold-eth";
+// ...
+if (!isConnected) return <RainbowKitCustomConnectButton />;
+```
+
+### 2. No wrong-network gate on the primary action
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+A wallet on Ethereum/Arbitrum/anything-not-Base still renders live Approve and Send Payout buttons. The header's
+`WrongNetworkDropdown` is not a gate — the user clicks Approve, signs against the wrong chain, and (because of #3)
+sees nothing at all.
+
+**Fix:** branch the action slot on chain before rendering the CTAs:
+```tsx
+const { chain } = useAccount();
+const { targetNetwork } = useTargetNetwork();
+const { switchChain } = useSwitchChain();
+
+if (chain?.id !== targetNetwork.id)
+  return (
+    <button className="btn btn-primary" onClick={() => switchChain({ chainId: targetNetwork.id })}>
+      Switch to {targetNetwork.name}
+    </button>
+  );
+```
+
+### 3. Raw wagmi `useWriteContract` instead of `useScaffoldWriteContract`
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:21`, used at `:38` and `:51`
+
+`writeContractAsync` from bare wagmi resolves the moment the wallet returns a hash — not at confirmation. So
+`setAmount("")`/`setMemo("")` at `:57-58` clear the form while the payout is still pending and may still revert.
+It also skips everything `useScaffoldWriteContract` provides: pre-flight `simulateContractWriteAndNotifyError`
+(would catch insufficient allowance/balance *before* the wallet prompt), the wrong-network notification, the
+"not deployed" guard, and tx-progress notifications via `useTransactor`.
+
+**Fix:** two hooks, one per contract, and drop the hand-passed `address`/`abi`:
+```tsx
+const { writeContractAsync: writeUsdc, isMining: isApproving } = useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "USDC" });
+const { writeContractAsync: writePayouts, isMining: isPaying } = useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "Payouts" });
+
+await writeUsdc({ functionName: "approve", args: [PAYOUTS.address, parseUnits(amount || "0", 6)] });
+await writePayouts({ functionName: "pay", args: [recipient, parseUnits(amount || "0", 6), memo] });
+```
+Clear the form only after the write resolves (which, with the scaffold hook, means confirmed).
+
+### 4. Failed and rejected transactions are silent
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46` and `:59-61`
+
+Both handlers `catch (e) { console.error(e); }`. A revert ("Payouts: transfer failed", insufficient allowance) or a
+user rejection produces zero UI feedback — the button re-enables and nothing else happens. Users will re-click and
+double-pay.
+
+**Fix:**
+```tsx
+import { getParsedError, notification } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth";
+// ...
+} catch (e) {
+  notification.error(getParsedError(e));
+}
+```
+(With #3 fixed, `useTransactor` already surfaces most of this; keep the catch for the rejection path.)
+
+### 5. USDC is hand-added to the autogenerated `deployedContracts.ts`
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:50` (entry `8453.USDC`)
+
+The file's own header says it is autogenerated and must not be edited. The next `yarn deploy` regenerates it from
+hardhat deployments, USDC vanishes, and `useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName: "USDC" })` starts silently
+returning nothing — balance shows `0`, approve breaks. This is a time bomb, not a style nit.
+
+**Fix:** move the entry verbatim into `externalContracts.ts`:
+```ts
+const externalContracts = {
+  8453: {
+    USDC: { address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913", abi: [/* the ABI as-is */] },
+  },
+} as const;
+```
+Then revert `deployedContracts.ts` to its generated state (keep `Payouts`, drop `USDC`), change
+`page.tsx:11` to import USDC from `externalContracts`, and confirm `yarn next:check-types` still passes.
+
+### 6. Recipient is a raw `<input type="text">`
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84`
+
+No ENS resolution, no checksum/format validation. `vitalik.eth` is passed straight through `recipient as \`0x${string}\``
+and never reaches the contract as an address. An empty string or a typo'd address goes to the wallet as-is; with #3
+there is no simulation to catch it either. Paying the wrong address in USDC is irreversible.
+
+**Fix:**
+```tsx
+import { AddressInput } from "@scaffold-ui/components";
+
+<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="Recipient address or ENS" />
+```
+and disable Send while `!isAddress(recipient)`.
+
+### 7. Hardcoded black page wrapper breaks light mode
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65`
+
+`className="min-h-screen bg-black text-white"` bypasses DaisyUI entirely. Light-mode users (and system-preference
+users — `ThemeProvider enableSystem` is on in `layout.tsx:19`) get a black page with a light header and footer, and
+the footer's `SwitchTheme` toggle appears to do nothing on this page. The `border-gray-700` at `:121` has the same
+problem.
+
+**Fix:** `className="min-h-screen bg-base-200 text-base-content"`, and `border-base-300` for the cards.
+
+### 8. Event history scans Base from genesis on every load
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:32`
+
+`fromBlock: 0n` forces `getLogs` over ~33.7M blocks. Public/rate-limited endpoints reject this outright; the feed
+either hangs or comes back empty, and it re-runs for every visitor. The hook already defaults to the contract's
+`deployedOnBlock` (`33712450`, present in `deployedContracts.ts:48`) when `fromBlock` is omitted.
+
+**Fix:** delete the `fromBlock: 0n` line and let the hook use `deployedOnBlock`. (Or pass `33712450n` explicitly.)
+
+### 9. `pollingInterval: 30000` on an L2
+`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24`
+
+Base blocks are 2s. A 30s poll means the balance and the payout feed can lag half a minute behind a confirmed
+transaction — the app reads as broken right after a user pays.
+
+**Fix:** `pollingInterval: 3000`, and refetch balance/feed on confirmation rather than relying on the poll alone.
+
+### 10. Production RPC is the shared scaffold Alchemy key
+`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:29` and `:32-35`; `packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConfig.tsx:20`
+
+`rpcOverrides` is empty (only a commented example), so unless `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` is actually set on the
+host, Base traffic falls back to `DEFAULT_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` — and `wagmiConfig` deliberately *deprioritizes* the
+default key behind the bare `http()` transport, i.e. the public rate-limited Base endpoint. Combined with #8 and
+`watch: true`, this will throttle on day one.
+
+**Fix:** set a real `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` in the Vercel/host env (it is in `.env.example` but only referenced
+in code — verify it is set on the host, not just committed), or add an explicit override:
+```ts
+rpcOverrides: {
+  [chains.base.id]: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL as string,
+},
+```
+
+---
+
+## Should-fix
+
+### 11. Buttons lock on `isPending`, not `isMining`
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101-102`, `:108-110`
+
+`isPending` from wagmi drops as soon as the wallet hands back a hash, so both buttons re-enable while the tx is
+still in the mempool — an easy accidental double-payout. `useScaffoldWriteContract` exposes `isMining`, which is
+held across `waitForTransactionReceipt` and cleared in a `finally` on both confirmation and rejection.
+
+**Fix:** with #3 applied, use `isApproving` / `isPaying` (the hooks' `isMining`) for `disabled`.
+
+### 12. `loading` class on a `btn` swallows the label
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101`, `:108`
+
+`` className={`btn btn-primary ${isPending ? "loading" : ""}`} `` replaces the whole button content with a spinner —
+mid-transaction the user sees two unlabeled buttons and cannot tell which one is working.
+
+**Fix:** keep the text, add an inline spinner:
+```tsx
+<button className="btn btn-primary" disabled={isApproving} onClick={handleApprove}>
+  {isApproving && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm" />}
+  Approve
+</button>
+```
+
+### 13. Approve and Send Payout are both live, always
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+There is no allowance read anywhere, so the UI never knows which step the user is on. New users will click Send
+first and get an opaque revert; returning users with a standing allowance are told to Approve again for nothing
+(an extra gas payment). The USDC ABI already includes `allowance` (`deployedContracts.ts:78-84`).
+
+**Fix:** read the allowance and render one CTA at a time:
+```tsx
+const { data: allowance } = useScaffoldReadContract({
+  contractName: "USDC",
+  functionName: "allowance",
+  args: [connectedAddress, PAYOUTS.address],
+});
+const needsApproval = (allowance ?? 0n) < parseUnits(amount || "0", 6);
+```
+Render Approve when `needsApproval`, Send Payout otherwise. Refetch the allowance after the approve confirms, and
+hold the button disabled until that refetch lands (local state, cleared in `finally` — not a `setTimeout`).
+
+### 14. Hand-rolled `shorten()` instead of `<Address/>`
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:13`, used at `:122` and `:124`
+
+Loses blockie avatar, ENS name/avatar, copy-to-clipboard, and the Basescan link. In a payouts feed, "did this go to
+the right person?" is the whole question — a bare `0x1234...5678` cannot answer it.
+
+**Fix:** `import { Address } from "@scaffold-ui/components";` and render `<Address address={payout.args.from} />` /
+`<Address address={payout.args.to} />`. Delete `shorten`.
+
+### 15. The Payouts contract address is never shown
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx` (page body)
+
+The page shows the user's own balance but never the contract they are approving and paying through. Users are asked
+to grant a USDC allowance to an address they cannot see or verify.
+
+**Fix:** render `<Address address={PAYOUTS.address} />` near the action area, labelled e.g. "Payouts contract".
+
+### 16. `--radius-field: 9999rem` makes pill-shaped inputs
+`packages/nextjs/styles/globals.css:36` and `:63`
+
+Fully-rounded text inputs and the amount field clip their content at the edges — visible on the recipient address,
+which is long. Present in both the light and dark theme blocks.
+
+**Fix:** set `--radius-field: 0.5rem;` in **both** `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` blocks (lines 36 and 63) — theme level,
+not per-component `rounded-*` overrides.
+
+### 17. Scaffold-ETH branding still throughout
+- `packages/nextjs/app/layout.tsx:11-12` — tab title is `"Scaffold-ETH 2 App"`, description `"Built with 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2"`.
+  Also `getMetadata.ts:8` templates every sub-page title as `"%s | Scaffold-ETH 2"`.
+- `packages/nextjs/components/Footer.tsx:50-74` — "Fork me" → scaffold-eth/se-2, "Built with ♥ at BuidlGuidl",
+  "Support" → the SE-2 Telegram invite. Real users will land in a stranger's support channel.
+- `README.md:1-15` — still the upstream SE-2 readme.
+- `packages/nextjs/public/favicon.png`, `thumbnail.jpg` — scaffold defaults; the thumbnail is the OG share image.
+
+**Fix:** product title/description in `layout.tsx`, product title template in `getMetadata.ts`, replace the three
+footer links with your own (or drop the row), rewrite the README, swap favicon + thumbnail.
+
+### 18. Phantom users cannot connect
+`packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:20-28`
+
+Phantom is not in the wallet list and is not in RainbowKit's defaults, so a large share of Base users have no way in.
+
+**Fix:**
+```ts
+import { phantomWallet } from "@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/wallets";
+const wallets = [metaMaskWallet, walletConnectWallet, phantomWallet, ledgerWallet, baseAccount, rainbowWallet, safeWallet, ...];
+```
+
+### 19. No mobile deep-link back to the wallet after a write
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:36-62`
+
+On WalletConnect mobile, tapping Approve or Send Payout fires the request and then nothing visible happens — the
+user must manually switch to their wallet app to find the pending signature. Most will assume it failed and re-tap.
+
+**Fix:** after calling the write (never before — navigating away first means the write never fires), redirect to the
+connected wallet's deep link, using the connector the user actually connected with, and skip it when already inside
+a wallet's in-app browser.
+
+### 20. Balance and feed are not refreshed after a payout
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:23-34`
+
+`usdcBalance` has no post-confirmation refetch; the feed relies on `watch` at the 30s interval from #9. After a
+successful payout the balance sits stale for up to half a minute.
+
+**Fix:** grab `refetch` from `useScaffoldReadContract` and call it (balance + allowance) after `handlePay` resolves.
+
+### 21. Confirm `Payouts` is verified on Basescan
+`packages/hardhat/deploy/00_deploy_payouts.ts`, deployed at `0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2`
+
+Could not check from here. Users are being asked to grant a USDC allowance to this contract; unverified bytecode
+reads as something to hide.
+
+**Fix:** `yarn verify --network base`, and confirm the constructor arg shows the Base USDC address.
+
+### 22. WalletConnect metadata says "scaffold-eth-2"
+`packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:49`
+
+`appName: "scaffold-eth-2"` is what the user sees in their mobile wallet's connection prompt — the moment trust is
+decided.
+
+**Fix:** set it to the product name (same string as the `layout.tsx` title).
+
+### 23. Shared default WalletConnect project ID
+`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:40`
+
+Falls back to the public scaffold project ID, which means shared rate limits and no analytics of your own.
+
+**Fix:** set `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` on the host and verify it is present in the production env.
+
+### 24. Event list keyed by array index
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:120-121`
+
+`key={i}` on a `watch`-updated list: new events prepend and React reuses the wrong rows. Cosmetic, but visible as
+rows flickering into the wrong content.
+
+**Fix:** `key={`${payout.log.transactionHash}-${payout.log.logIndex}`}`.
+
+---
+
+## Open questions
+
+1. Is `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` actually set in the production host env, or only in `.env.example`? (#10)
+2. Should approve request an exact amount (current behavior) or unlimited? Exact is safer but costs a second tx per payout.
+3. Is the Payouts contract verified on Basescan already? (#21)

